1
00:06:48,750 --> 00:06:54,750
Three Great Laff Stars ! . . . more gags and gals . . . more songs and dances !

2
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:43,500
A Day at the Races is a comedy, music film directed by Sam Wood.

3
00:20:26,250 --> 00:20:32,250
Doctor Hugo Hackenbush, Tony, and Stuffy try and save Judy's sanitarium by
winning a big race with a finicky horse owned by Judy's boyfriend Gil.

4
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:21,000
There are a few problems.

5
00:34:03,750 --> 00:34:09,750
Hackenbush, who was recently put in charge of the sanitarium,
isn't really a doctor, he's a veterinarian.

6
00:40:52,500 --> 00:40:58,500
Dr. Hugo Z. Hackenbush, played by Groucho Marx.

7
00:47:41,250 --> 00:47:47,250
Tony, played by Chico Marx.

8
00:54:30,000 --> 00:54:36,000
Stuffy, played by Harpo Marx.

9
01:01:18,750 --> 01:01:24,750
Gil Stewart, played by Allan Jones.

10
01:08:07,500 --> 01:08:13,500
Judy Standish, played by Maureen O'Sullivan.

11
01:14:56,250 --> 01:15:02,250
Emily Upjohn, played by Margaret Dumont.

12
01:21:45,000 --> 01:21:51,000
A Day at the Races is a 1937 American comedy film, and the seventh film starring the Marx Brothers
(Groucho, Harpo and Chico), with Allan Jones, Maureen O'Sullivan and Margaret Dumont.

13
01:28:33,750 --> 01:28:39,750
Like their 1935 Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer feature A Night at
the Opera, this film was a major hit.

14
01:35:22,500 --> 01:35:28,500
The film explores themes of veterinarian, musical, femme fatale.

15
01:42:11,250 --> 01:42:17,250
The tone is lighthearted.
